            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-58055-libnghttp2-14",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-58055 medium vulnerability for libnghttp2-14 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "nghttp2's nghttpx proxy through 1.69.0 forwards an HTTP/1.1 Upgrade request that also carries a Content-Length header and body onto reusable keep-alive backend connections, re-adding the Upgrade and Connection headers while passing Content-Length verbatim. A backend that resolves the resulting ambiguous message in the attacker's favor enables HTTP request/response smuggling and cross-client response-queue poisoning."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-58055",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-58055\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libnghttp2-14\nVersion: 1.70.0-1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-58055](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-58055)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-58055**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libnghttp2-14  | 1.70.0-1  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-58055](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-58055)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libnghttp2-14@1.70.0-1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=nghttp2"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-56433-login.defs",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-56433 low vulnerability for login.defs package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "shadow-utils (aka shadow) 4.4 through 4.17.0 establishes a default /etc/subuid behavior (e.g., uid 100000 through 165535 for the first user account) that can realistically conflict with the uids of users defined on locally administered networks, potentially leading to account takeover, e.g., by leveraging newuidmap for access to an NFS home directory (or same-host resources in the case of remote logins by these local network users). NOTE: it may also be argued that system administrators should not have assigned uids, within local networks, that are within the range that can occur in /etc/subuid."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-56433",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-56433\nSeverity: low\nPackage: login.defs\nVersion: 1:4.19.3-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2024-56433](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-56433)",
