            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-15534-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-15534 medium vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Perl versions through 5.45.1 have out-of-bounds heap reads and writes during regular expression matching via an undersized superlinear cache in S_regmatch.  The regex engine's superlinear cache holds one bit per subject position for each participating WHILEM node, so the bit count is the subject length plus one times the number of nodes. Nothing checks that product for positive overflow of the signed 32-bit count: a 286331153 byte subject matched against a pattern with 15 participating nodes stores the count as 14, leaving a two byte cache. The cache is then indexed from the real match position and node number, so reads go past the end of the allocation, and on failure CACHEsayNO sets a bit past it.  A caller that matches an attacker controlled subject of this size against a pattern of this shape can crash the process or corrupt heap memory."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-15534",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-15534\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.42.3-1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-15534](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-15534)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-15534**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | perl-base  | 5.42.3-1  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-15534](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-15534)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/perl-base@5.42.3-1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-18508-tar",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-18508 medium vulnerability for tar package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in GNU tar. When extracting an archive with the --one-top-level option, hardlink targets are not confined to the designated top-level directory and may resolve relative to the extraction working directory. A crafted archive can create hardlinks that escape the intended boundary and, when combined with a preexisting symbolic link under the working directory, may allow writing outside that boundary during a single extraction."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-18508",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-18508\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: tar\nVersion: 1.35+dfsg-5\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-18508](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-18508)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-18508**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | tar  | 1.35+dfsg-5  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-18508](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-18508)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/tar@1.35%2Bdfsg-5?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.4"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-42250-libbz2-1.0",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-42250 medium vulnerability for libbz2-1.0 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "bzip2 contains an off‑by‑one error in the bzip2recover utility. When processing a specially crafted file, the application performs an out‑of‑bounds write to a global buffer, resulting in memory corruption and a crash (denial of service).  This issue was fixed in bzip2 patch 35d122a3df8b0cc4082a4d89fdc6ee99f375fe67"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-42250",
